# Web App Intelligence

Behavioral model / digital twin of web apps. **Not** a scraper, chatbot, Playwright-generator-only tool, or AI browser agent.

## Source of truth

- Full architecture: `docs/MASTER_CONTEXT.md` — read before architectural decisions, schema changes, or roadmap jumps. Do not ask the user to paste it.
- Sequential checklist: `docs/STEP1_CHECKLIST.md` — current Phase/Gate work order.
- Post-MVP scenario audit (after Lab L1–L11 + Phase 14 only): `docs/POST_MVP_SCENARIO_CHECKLIST.md`. Do not execute that catalog during L1 or as Step 1 scope.
- Product destination: `docs/PRODUCT_UI_VISION.md` (analysis) and `docs/mockups/` (the screens themselves). Read the vision doc before contract/schema/persistence decisions or dashboard work; open images only for pixel detail. Mockups inform **what Step 1 must retain**; they do not override `docs/MASTER_CONTEXT.md` or the active checklist item, and they do not authorize building Step 2–6 surfaces (assistant, graph, test gen, monitoring, automation builder) early.
- When a Step 1 choice would make a mockup screen impossible or force a re-crawl later, say so at the time and name the screen.

## Implementation ownership

The user implements application code by default to retain understanding and control.

- **Do not** write or edit application/source code, migrations, configs that run the system, or tests unless the user **explicitly** asks you to implement that item.
- **Do** answer questions, review their code, explain design tradeoffs, and suggest next checklist items.
- **May** create/update instruction or docs text the user needs for prompting/context (rules, checklists, how-to-prompt) without being asked each time.

## Core principles

- **Discover once, structure, reuse** — all products share one evidence-backed model
- Prefer: deterministic code → cache → DB/graph → vector search → local AI → cloud LLM last
- Every important fact needs **provenance** and an evidence status: OBSERVED | VERIFIED | INFERRED | STALE | FAILED
- Safety gates all risky browser actions; never auto-run destructive/financial actions
- Generalize routes/components/workflows; avoid state explosion
- Strong TypeScript; keep modules testable; preserve data later phases need

## Stack (Step 1)

TypeScript, Node.js, Playwright (Chromium only), PostgreSQL (+ JSONB), React/Next.js dashboard, Docker. No Neo4j, multi-browser, or LLM-centric control in Step 1.

## Current position

**STEP 1 — Discovery Engine** (not Step 2+). Follow `docs/STEP1_CHECKLIST.md`. Immediate path: Discovery Contract → repo/Postgres → BrowserSession → DiscoverySession → open URL → persist evidence-backed initial state snapshot.

Scope work to the active Phase 0–14 item. Do not build assistant, knowledge graph products, test generation, monitoring, or automation until asked and prerequisites exist.

## Conflict handling

If a request conflicts with `docs/MASTER_CONTEXT.md`, say so and explain consequences before changing the design.
